{"hash":"a5b90372fb1f4c2d","index":24,"payload":{"attempt":0,"kind":"RAW_PROPOSAL","raw":"Kr=1 confirms the prediction exactly. Under H03, H04, H10, and H29 (each satisfied by only 2 of the 4 unassigned vectors), Zn=1 and Rc=1 already forced those symbols to occupy *both* satisfying vectors for that hypothesis (since vectors are distinct under the bijection). That leaves only non-satisfying vectors for Kr and Ly \u2014 so Kr=1 is strictly impossible under any of those four, not just unlikely. They're logically falsified, not merely downweighted. Only H22 (NOT p1 OR p2), which is true on all four remaining vectors, permits Kr=1. All posterior mass collapses to H22.\n\n```json\n{\"type\":\"SUFFICIENCY\",\"final_hypothesis\":\"H22\",\"confidence\":0.99}\n```","ts":1787359224.503032},"prev":"0d454c5e0a27ea0a"}
